# Agent Autonomy: Verified Execution

**Core Directive:** No code change is complete until it has been verified. Use available tools to prove the change works as intended before handing back control to the user.

---

## Stack Reference

This is a minimal **SvelteKit 2 / Svelte 5 (Runes)** app deployed on **Vercel**.

| Layer | Detail |
|---|---|
| Rendering | Fully SSR — no client-side fetching. All data flows through `load()` in `+page.server.ts` |
| Database | **Upstash Redis** (HTTP client via `@upstash/redis`). Single key: `daily_cache` |
| AI | **Gemini 2.5 Flash** (`@google/genai`) with `googleSearch` grounding tool |
| Cron | Vercel Cron — `GET /api/cron` at `0 0 * * *` UTC, authenticated by `Bearer CRON_SECRET` |
| Styling | Scoped CSS-in-Svelte (no Tailwind, no CSS framework) |
| Server-only modules | `$lib/server/redis.ts`, `$lib/server/content.ts` — never import these on the client |
| Preview route | `/preview` — dev-only; throws 404 in production; used to test Gemini output and layout |

---

## 1. Mandatory Post-Change Verification

### UI / Component changes (`ArticleView.svelte`, `+page.svelte`, `+layout.svelte`)
- Open the browser tool and navigate to `http://localhost:5173` (or the active dev server port)
- Take a screenshot and verify the layout renders correctly
- Check that Svelte 5 Runes (`$props()`, `$state()`, `$derived()`) are used correctly — never use the legacy `export let` prop syntax
- Run `npx svelte-check` and confirm zero new type or component errors

### API / Cron changes (`src/routes/api/cron/+server.ts`)
- The cron endpoint requires an `Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET>` header — always include it in test `curl` calls
- Test with: `curl -s -X GET http://localhost:5173/api/cron -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET"`
- Verify the response is `{ success: true }` and that Redis was written by running a follow-up read via `src/lib/server/redis.ts` logic or a quick script
- If calling Gemini, confirm `groundingMetadata.groundingChunks` is present in the response (indicates successful web search grounding)

### Redis changes (`src/lib/server/redis.ts`, any `redis.set` / `redis.get` call)
- After writing, read back the `daily_cache` key and log its shape: `{ content, sources, metadata, updated_at }`
- Confirm `updated_at` is a valid ISO timestamp and `sources` is a non-empty array when grounding was active

### Markdown / content pipeline changes (`src/lib/server/content.ts`)
- Run a quick Node script or use the `/preview` route to render a sample markdown string through `markdownToSafeHtml()`
- Verify `h1`–`h6` headings render correctly (they are explicitly allowlisted in `sanitize-html`)
- Confirm no raw HTML tags appear as escaped text in the output

### Server load changes (`src/routes/+page.server.ts`, `src/routes/preview/+page.server.ts`)
- Reload the page and confirm the `data` object contains `{ content: string, sources: [], updatedAt }` with no undefined fields
- Run `npx svelte-check` after any TypeScript signature change

### Type / logic changes
- Run `npx tsc --noEmit` or `npx svelte-check` before marking the task done
- Zero new errors required — do not hand back with outstanding type regressions

